> > What's "fropi"?
>
> It isn't anything, but the morphology rules don't care which gismu are
> defined and which are not.

Nor do they care about whether the cmavo that falls off a brivla makes any 
sense grammatically. This one doesn't; "ne" has to be followed by a term, and 
a term can't begin with a brivla. Of course you could say "zo ne fropi", 
which is grammatical.

